{{!--
    One stock row, as columns: item, quantity available, price, actions.

    Two actions, not four. Where the goods go is asked once in the Buy dialog rather
    than encoded in three icons a player has to learn apart.

    One action per row: everything a player buys goes through the cart, and the cart
    is checked out once.

    A control that cannot act is disabled and says why on hover, rather than being
    absent. An absent button reads as "this shop does not do that"; a disabled one
    with a reason reads as "not right now, and here is what would change it".

    Every flag it needs is precomputed on the row itself: the partial renders at two
    depths, so `../` would mean different things in each.
--}}
{{!-- `data-search` is built in the context rather than read back out of the
      markup: the filter then never depends on what the row happens to render, and
      matching stays a substring test on a string that is already lowercased. --}}
<div class="merchant-shop-item{{#if card}} merchant-shop-card is-{{cardSize}}{{/if}}{{#if outOfStock}} is-out{{/if}}{{#if reserved}} is-reserved{{/if}}" data-item-id="{{id}}" data-owner="{{owner}}"
     data-search="{{searchKey}}"{{#if gridStyle}} style="{{gridStyle}}"{{/if}}>
    <img src="{{img}}" alt="">

    <div class="merchant-shop-item-copy">
        <strong>{{name}}</strong>
        {{!-- Kind, then rarity where there is one. Most of a shop is ordinary objects
              with no rarity at all, and printing "Mundane" beside every torch would
              spend the line on the rows that need it least. --}}
        <span>{{typeLabel}}{{#if rarity}} · <em data-rarity="{{rarityKey}}">{{rarity}}</em>{{/if}}{{#if weightLabel}} · {{weightLabel}}{{/if}}</span>
        {{!-- **Only on a card.** A counter row is one line per thing and a paragraph in it
              would make the list unreadable; a card is a page entry and the description is
              most of what makes it one. Capped in the context, not here. --}}
        {{#if blurb}}<p class="merchant-shop-card-blurb">{{blurb}}</p>{{/if}}
    </div>

    {{!-- Unlimited reads as a symbol, anything else as a number, so the column does
          not move between stock policies. A GM edits the number in place, which sets
          both what is there and what a restocking inventory refills to. --}}
    {{!-- **No quantity in a catalogue.** A warehouse's stock level is not a fact the
          reader of a catalogue needs, and a shelf that is infinite by default has no
          honest number to show anyway. The column goes rather than showing a symbol
          nobody asked about. --}}
    {{#unless catalogue}}
        {{#if canEditStock}}
            <div class="merchant-shop-item-qty merchant-shop-qty-editable" data-edit-stock="{{id}}"
                 data-tooltip="{{qtyTooltip}} — double-click to change">
                <small>{{localize "coffee-pub-merchant.row.quantityAbbr"}}</small><strong>{{qtyLabel}}</strong>
            </div>
        {{else}}
            <div class="merchant-shop-item-qty" data-tooltip="{{qtyTooltip}}">
                <small>{{localize "coffee-pub-merchant.row.quantityAbbr"}}</small><strong>{{qtyLabel}}</strong>
            </div>
        {{/if}}
    {{/unless}}

    {{!-- **The cell carries the editor, not the figure in it.** An unpriced row has no
          figure to double-click, and that is precisely the row that most needs one:
          without a price it cannot go on the slate, so the slate's own price control
          can never be reached. GM only, and the same double-click as the quantity
          beside it. --}}
    <div class="merchant-shop-item-price{{#if canPrice}} merchant-shop-qty-editable{{/if}}"
         {{#if canPrice}}data-edit-list-price="{{id}}" data-price-each="{{priceEach}}"
         data-tooltip="{{listPriceTooltip}}"{{/if}}>
        {{!-- A negotiate inventory is checked *first*, before any figure. Once a price has
              been agreed `priceLabel` would otherwise have something in it, and showing
              it here would publish a private agreement to the next player who opened
              the shop. The tooltip is GM-only and the context decides that, so a player
              inspecting the markup finds nothing to read either. --}}
        {{#if isUnpricedInventory}}
            <em class="merchant-shop-negotiate"
                {{#if negotiateTooltip}}data-tooltip="{{negotiateTooltip}}"{{/if}}>{{localize "coffee-pub-merchant.row.negotiate"}}</em>
        {{else if priceLabel}}
            <strong>{{priceLabel}}</strong>
        {{else}}
            <em class="merchant-shop-unpriced"
                {{#unless canPrice}}data-tooltip="{{localize "coffee-pub-merchant.row.noPriceTooltip"}}"{{/unless}}>{{localize "coffee-pub-merchant.row.noPrice"}}</em>
        {{/if}}
    </div>

    {{#if busy}}
        <div class="merchant-shop-row-actions">
            <span class="merchant-shop-blocked"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-notch fa-spin"></i></span>
        </div>
    {{!-- A negotiate row adds like any other. "Ask" was a dead end: it named the
          thing to do and then left you to do it somewhere else. Putting it on the
          slate at TBD is what asking *is* -- the item is now between the two of you,
          and the price is the part still outstanding. --}}
    {{else}}
        <div class="merchant-shop-row-actions">
            {{!-- One action. There was a Buy alongside this that purchased the row
                  outright, and it was never fewer prompts than the cart: pick a
                  quantity, pick a destination, confirm, either way. Two paths through
                  the same money, and two places for them to disagree. --}}
            {{!-- `addAction` so a row can serve both sides: the inventories add to the
                  buying half, your own pack adds to the selling half. Same row, same
                  gesture, one word different. --}}
            <button type="button" class="blacksmith-window-btn-secondary merchant-shop-cart-add"
                    data-action="{{#if addAction}}{{addAction}}{{else}}addToCart{{/if}}" data-item-id="{{id}}"
                    {{#unless canCart}}disabled{{/unless}} data-tooltip="{{cartTooltip}}">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i>
            </button>
            {{#if canRemove}}
                {{!-- GM only. Zero is out of stock, which is a state a shop is in;
                      this is the inventory no longer carrying the thing at all. --}}
                <button type="button" class="blacksmith-window-btn-secondary merchant-shop-remove"
                        data-action="removeStock" data-item-id="{{id}}"
                        data-tooltip="{{localize "coffee-pub-merchant.row.removeTooltip"}}">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark"></i>
                </button>
            {{/if}}
        </div>
    {{/if}}
</div>
